  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Circular Solutions for the Food and Beverage Sector to Tackle Plastic Pollution in Cambodia(Plastic IP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The use of single-use plastics (SUPs) has rapidly accelerated in Cambodia, particularly in the food and beverage (F&amp;B) and tourism sectors, resulting in negative impacts on human health, the environment, and the economy. The Royal Government of Cambodia has developed various policies and strategies to support a circular economy (CE). However, their implementation is hindered by a lack of enforceable regulations, financial instruments, capacity, and public awareness. To address these challenges,</narrative>
  </description>
